/E (Control Gap : Ask of any process: can one person initiate, approve, and release? If the answer is yes, you have found an opportunity.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
428 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 230 0 R
/E (The act is only half a fraud. The other half is the effort to keep it from being seen.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
429 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 230 0 R
/E (Rakul printed a vendor letter on a letterhead he had copied, requesting the change of bank details, and filed it in the vendor folder. Should anyone ask, the paperwork existed. At every month-end, he made sure he was the one preparing the vendor reconciliation, so the one person who could have spotted the problem was the one person writing the report on it.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
430 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 230 0 R
/E (This is what concealment looks like in practice. Almost every fraud comes with some form of cover-up, and a forged or altered paper trail remains the favourite, even in a digital age.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
