/P 230 0 R
/E (This is how most frauds surface. The honest supplier, wondering why a payment never arrived, asked a simple question, and one question was enough to unravel eighteen months of work.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
436 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 230 0 R
/E (Detection method matters enormously. The ACFE found that fraud can be uncovered up to four times faster through active detection than through passive means. Active detection means a deliberate check such as surveillance, monitoring, or reconciliation. Passive detection means being told, stumbling across it, or being notified by the police.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
437 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 230 0 R
/E (Data analytics, exception reports, independent reconciliations and accessible reporting channels can all help surface these issues earlier. But the information must reach someone willing and able to act on it.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
