/P 234 0 R
/E (An organisation may have a well-defined approval process, but if employees bypass it to save time or managers approve things without looking at the details, the control is not really serving its purpose. A control should not just look good in a policy document. It should work consistently, even when there is pressure to meet deadlines or achieve business targets. It is also important to check whether people understand why the control exists, rather than simply treating it as another step in the process. )
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [12]
>>
